  "description": "NVIDIA MAISI is a medical-imaging NIM for generating synthetic 3D CT volumes and paired segmentation labels from requested body regions, anatomies, voxel spacing, and output-size controls. The current NVIDIA documentation says MAISI 1.0.1 is an accelerated release, exposes /v1/maisi/run, and returns ZIP archives containing generated imaging artifacts. This Forge manifest records the existing digest-verified regional latest mirrors and keeps the UI scoped to nonclinical synthetic-data and research workflows. MAISI must not be used for clinical diagnosis, treatment planning, patient-specific decisions, or evaluation of real patient imaging.",
